+- dependency: happy-dom
+- dependency: todomvc-common
+- dependency: todomvc-app-css
+## Outbound
+- outbound: none
diff --git a/features/managing-todos.feature b/features/managing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a15c0f3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/managing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+Feature: Managing todos
+  As a visitor
+  I want to add, complete, edit, and remove todos
+  So that I can track what needs to be done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open with no stored todos
+
+  Scenario: An empty todo list hides the list section and the footer
+    Then the todo list section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Submitting a new todo appends it and clears the input
+    When the visitor submits a new todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the new todo input is empty
+    And the counter reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: A blank title is not added
+    When the visitor submits a new todo "   "
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace around a new title is trimmed
+    When the visitor submits a new todo "  Buy milk  "
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo marks it completed
+    Given the todo list contains an active todo "Buy milk"
+    When the visitor completes "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    And the counter reads "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: The counter pluralizes the item count
+    Given the todo list contains active todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the visitor completes "Walk the dog"
+    Then the counter reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Marking all todos as complete completes every todo
+    Given the todo list contains active todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the visitor marks all todos as complete
+    Then "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    And "Walk the dog" is marked completed
+    And the mark-all control is checked
+
+  Scenario: Uncompleting one todo unchecks the mark-all control
+    Given the todo list contains completed todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the visitor reactivates "Buy milk"
+    Then the mark-all control is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo saves the new title
+    Given the todo list contains an active todo "Buy milk"
+    When the visitor edits "Buy milk" to "Buy oat milk"
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo to a blank title destroys it
+    Given the todo list contains an active todo "Buy milk"
+    When the visitor edits "Buy milk" to "   "
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Escape during editing discards the change
+    Given the todo list contains an active todo "Buy milk"
+    When the visitor starts editing "Buy milk"
+    And the visitor changes the edit text to "Buy oat milk"
+    And the visitor presses Escape
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Destroying a todo removes it
+    Given the todo list contains an active todo "Buy milk"
+    When the visitor destroys "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes only completed todos
+    Given the todo list contains an active todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo list contains a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the visitor clears completed todos
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Walk the dog"
+    And the mark-all control is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: The clear completed control hides when no todo is completed
+    Given the todo list contains an active todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the clear completed control is hidden
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1516c68
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+Feature: Persisting todos
+  As a visitor
+  I want my todos saved to localStorage
+  So that they survive a page reload
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open with no stored todos
+
+  Scenario: Todos and their completion state survive a reload
+    Given the visitor has added an active todo "Buy milk"
+    And the visitor has added a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the visitor reloads the app
+    Then "Buy milk" is marked active
+    And "Walk the dog" is marked completed
+    And the counter reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Stored todos use the todos-vanillajs key with id, title, and completed fields
+    When the visitor submits a new todo "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage key "todos-vanillajs" holds a todo with the title "Buy milk"
+    And that stored todo has an id field
+    And that stored todo has a completed field set to false
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given the visitor has added an active todo "Buy milk"
+    And the visitor starts editing "Buy milk"
+    When the visitor reloads the app
+    Then "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..001595e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+Feature: Filtering todos by route
+  As a visitor
+  I want to filter todos by their state
+  So that I can focus on what is active or completed
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open with an active todo "Buy milk" and a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: The default route shows every todo
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+    And the "All" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The active route shows only active todos
+    When the visitor opens the "#/active" route
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Walk the dog"
+    And the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The completed route shows only completed todos
+    When the visitor opens the "#/completed" route
+    Then the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Buy milk"
+    And the "Completed" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo on the active route hides it
+    Given the visitor is on the "#/active" route
+    When the visitor completes "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list does not contain "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: The active filter survives a reload
+    Given the visitor is on the "#/active" route
+    When the visitor reloads the app
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Walk the dog"
+    And the "Active" filter link is selected
